  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two radionctive substances $A$ and $B$ have decay constants $5 \\lambda$ and $\\lambda$ respectively. At $t=0,$ they have the same number of nuclei. The ratio of number of nuclei of $A$ to that of $B$ will be $(1 / e)^{2}$\r\nafter a time interval of",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rqp7S",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "v35ra",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 \\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jTsZC",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3 \\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AK8Pd",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4 \\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that\n$N=N_{0} e^{-\\lambda t}$\nFor $A$,\n$N_{A}=N_{0} e^{-5 \\lambda_{L}}$\nFor $B$,\n$N_{B}=N_{0} e^{-\\lambda t}$\nGiven,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{N_{A}}{N_{B}} &=\\frac{1}{e^{2}} \\\\\n\\frac{N}{N_{B}} &=\\frac{1}{e^{4 \\lambda t}} \\\\\nt &=\\frac{1}{2 \\lambda}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
